IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ita-types`
IMPORT `ita-rates`
IMPORT `ita-reliefs`
IMPORT `cpf-contributions`
IMPORT `cpf-wages-year`
IMPORT `sg-household`

-- IRAS worked examples against the household encoding: NUMBERS ONLY.
--
-- Every expected value is a figure from a worked example on one of IRAS's pages, fetched 2026-11-24 (the pages' addresses are in FINDINGS.md section 4);
-- the comment above each assertion names the example and the page by a short name. The table of examples and the mapping notes are kept outside
-- this repository: they are a third party's figures table. No expected value was edited to match the code: a failing assertion is a finding
-- (FINDINGS.md section 4 lists what the first run found, and what was changed in the Income Tax Act encoding as a result).
-- Income year 2025 (YA 2026) unless the comment says otherwise.
-- The CPF relief that an IRAS example gives as a figure is passed in through `the relief breakdown given CPF` / `the position of an adult`; where
-- the household computes CPF itself, the pay layout is 12 equal whole-dollar ordinary wages plus one additional wage in December.
-- Dates: each adult is born in December, so the age at 31 December of the income year is the income year minus the year of birth.
-- Part-year (Cheong) is eleven months of ordinary wages and a zero January: the year function needs twelve entries.

`a month of pay` ow aw MEANS `My pay in one month` OF ow, aw

-- ---- accessors: unwrap a MAYBE position, -1 where the encoding does not cover the case ----

GIVEN p IS A MAYBE (A `One adult's position`)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income tax in` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0 MINUS 1
    WHEN JUST q THEN q's `income tax`

GIVEN p IS A MAYBE (A `One adult's position`)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the employee CPF in` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0 MINUS 1
    WHEN JUST q THEN q's `employee CPF`

GIVEN p IS A MAYBE (A `One adult's position`)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the assessable income in` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0 MINUS 1
    WHEN JUST q THEN q's `assessable income`

GIVEN p IS A MAYBE (A `One adult's position`)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reliefs allowed in` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0 MINUS 1
    WHEN JUST q THEN q's `reliefs allowed, after the s 39A cap`

GIVEN p IS A MAYBE (A `One adult's position`)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the chargeable income in` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0 MINUS 1
    WHEN JUST q THEN q's `chargeable income`

GIVEN p IS A MAYBE (A `One adult's position`)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax before the rebate in` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0 MINUS 1
    WHEN JUST q THEN q's `tax before the parenthood rebate`

GIVEN p IS A MAYBE (A `One adult's position`)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rebate used in` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0 MINUS 1
    WHEN JUST q THEN q's `parenthood rebate used`

GIVEN p IS A MAYBE (A `One adult's position`)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rebate carried forward in` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0 MINUS 1
    WHEN JUST q THEN q's `parenthood rebate carried forward`

-- The adult in position 1 or 2 (position 2 falls back to the first adult if there is none).
GIVEN h IS A `Household`
      who IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Adult of the household`
`the adult in position` MEANS
    IF   who EQUALS 1
    THEN h's `the first adult`
    ELSE CONSIDER h's `the second adult`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN h's `the first adult`
         WHEN JUST a THEN a

-- The Individual relief facts the household builds for an adult, with the CPF relief passed in (as an IRAS example states it).
GIVEN h IS A `Household`
      who IS A NUMBER
      cpf IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Relief breakdown`
`the relief breakdown given CPF` MEANS
    `the personal reliefs for YA` (h's `the income year` PLUS 1) `, resident:` TRUE `:` (`the relief facts of an adult` h who (`the adult in position` h who) cpf)

GIVEN y IS A `My year of work`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the CPF of the year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my employee CPF for the year` y
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0 MINUS 1
    WHEN JUST n THEN n

